---
// The QA skill's showcase, and the reference implementation every other skill
// diagram should follow.
//
// Two rules it establishes:
//   1. Each step is a `.hotspot` group carrying `data-detail`, which must match
//      an `id` in the card's `details` frontmatter. Card.astro's script pairs
//      them: click a step and the flow write-up opens, scrolled to that step.
//   2. It shares the `.topology` classes with every other diagram so they read
//      as one visual language and track the theme.
//
// The return leg is a hotspot too — how a rejected fix is scoped is a real step
// in this process, not a connector. It needs an explicit transparent hit area
// because a stroked path is only clickable on the stroke itself.
//
// Source facts: src/content/cards/qa.md, docs/context/testing.md.
---

<figure class="card-diagram">
  <div class="card-diagram-scroll">
    <svg
      class="topology"
      viewBox="0 0 820 300"
      role="img"
      aria-labelledby="qa-loop-title qa-loop-desc"
      xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"
      fill="none"
    >
      <title id="qa-loop-title">How work gets checked before it counts as finished</title>
      <desc id="qa-loop-desc">
        A six-step cycle. One: the feature specification and the expected results
        are written before any planning or building starts. Two: the coding agent
        plans and builds it. Three: scripted automated tests run before a human
        looks at anything. Four: I test the output by hand and compare it against
        the expected results. Five: anything that does not match goes back to the
        agent as a list of narrowly scoped fixes, with the session context kept concise so
        it cannot hallucinate, and the cycle returns to step two. Six: once every
        expected result is met, the documentation is updated and then compacted
        to a context budget.
      </desc>

      <defs>
        <marker id="qa-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse">
          <path class="arrow-head" d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" stroke="none" />
        </marker>
      </defs>

      <!-- the return leg, drawn above the row so it never crosses the flow -->
      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="feedback" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 5, fixes go back specific and small — open the explanation">
        <rect x="296" y="24" width="436" height="38" fill="transparent" />
        <path class="link ephemeral-link" d="M716,76 L716,46 L308,46 L308,76" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />
        <text class="wire" x="512" y="38" text-anchor="middle">5 · Lists of specific fix · context kept concise so it can't invent</text>
      </g>

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="spec" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 1, specification and expected results first — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="15" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="29" y="100">1 · Spec first</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="118">what it must do, and the</text>
        <text class="sub" x="29" y="134">results I expect to see</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M195,116 L217,116" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="build" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 2, the agent plans and builds — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="219" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="233" y="100">2 · Agent builds</text>
        <text class="sub" x="233" y="118">planning and building,</text>
        <text class="sub" x="233" y="134">and fixing</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M399,116 L421,116" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="tests" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 3, automated tests run before I look — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="423" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="437" y="100">3 · Automated tests</text>
        <text class="sub" x="437" y="118">scripted checks run before</text>
        <text class="sub" x="437" y="134">I look at anything</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M603,116 L625,116" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="manual" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 4, Manual Testing — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="627" y="76" width="178" height="80" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="641" y="100">4 · Manual Testing</text>
        <text class="sub" x="641" y="118">actual output against the</text>
        <text class="sub" x="641" y="134">expected results</text>
      </g>

      <path class="link" d="M716,156 L716,206" marker-end="url(#qa-arrow)" />
      <text class="wire accent" x="726" y="186">all results met</text>

      <g class="hotspot" data-detail="docs" role="button" tabindex="0" aria-label="Step 6, documentation updated then compacted — open the explanation">
        <rect class="node" x="627" y="206" width="178" height="70" rx="10" />
        <text class="label" x="641" y="230">6 · Docs updated</text>
        <text class="sub" x="641" y="248">then compacted to a</text>
        <text class="sub" x="641" y="264">context budget</text>
      </g>

      <text class="wire accent" x="15" y="234">Nothing is approved by whoever built it</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="254">the same rule an engineering team runs on — it does not</text>
      <text class="wire" x="15" y="270">stop applying because the builder is a machine</text>
    </svg>
  </div>
  <figcaption class="card-diagram-caption">
    Click any step to read what it means.
  </figcaption>
</figure>
